                "title": "insertion of iqac objectives",
                "meta_data": {
                    "about": "The Internal Quality Assurance Cell (IQAC) was established in 2004 as per the guidelines of the National Assessment and Accreditation Council (NAAC) to ensure continuous improvement in the overall performance of the institution. The IQAC serves as a central body that coordinates and monitors quality enhancement initiatives across various departments and functions of the college.",
                    "objectives": [
                    "To develop a system for conscious, consistent and catalytic action to improve the academic and administrative performance of the institution.",
                    "To promote measures for institutional functioning towards quality enhancement through internalization of quality culture and institutionalization of best practices.",
                    "To provide a sound basis for decision-making to improve institutional functioning by facilitating the creation of a learner-centric environment.",
                    "To act as a dynamic system for quality changes in higher education by fostering a culture of excellence and innovation."
                    ]
                    },
                "original_data": null
            },
